ml435's [span-census] proved the 16GB FEX band fills by LIVE DEMAND, not leaks:
~74 live guest threads x ~200MB (2-3 x 64MB spans + code buffers) consumed the
whole band, after which code-buffer allocation failed and Crashpad killed the
webhelper right after BrowserReady.

16MB spans cut the per-thread span footprint 4x (~48MB worst case); with the
ml389 VA diet and exact-aligned maps this puts 74 threads at ~3.5GB.
LARGE_PAGE_SIZE_SHIFT drops to 24 to keep SPAN_SIZE / LARGE_PAGE_SIZE >= 1;
blocks in (16MB, 64MB] shift to the huge path, which maps them at exact size —
a VA improvement over carving them from a 64MB span.

Verified ml436: zero failed band scans.

